    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n87300" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προεν-τυγχάνω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>encounter, meet first,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.363
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>BJ</u>
				5.6.5
			</span></i>, al.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῇ ἄγρᾳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ael.
					<u>NA</u>
					4.13
				</span></i>
			; <i>come in contact with first,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῖς πράγμασι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.1122b
				</span></i>
			: pf.
			part.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-εντετυχηκώς</span>”
				<i>previously acquainted with,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					17(1).501
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>intercede with first,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.547
			</span></i>; <i>have audience of first,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρέσβεις π. τῇ βουλῇ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Nic.</u>
					10
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄψις π. αὐτοῦ τῆς
			φωνῆς</span> an appearance which <i>spoke for</i> him
				<i>before</i> he opened his mouth, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Pomp.</u>
				2
			</span></i>.</div>
